**History of Present Illness (HPI):**
Alexis reports numbness and tingling in her right hand, which started 6 months ago. She experiences pain and stiffness, particularly when performing tasks that involve repetitive hand movements, such as typing on a keyboard. She has also noticed difficulty gripping objects and occasional numbness in her thumb and index finger. These symptoms are persistent throughout the day, but they are worse in the evenings. She mentions that her symptoms do not significantly affect her sleep but have impacted her ability to perform tasks at work. She uses ibuprofen (400 mg) twice daily to manage pain.

**Review of Systems (ROS):**
- **Neurological:** Numbness and tingling in the right hand, difficulty gripping objects, occasional numbness in the thumb and index finger.
